.TH rev-stealth 1  "rev-stealth 1.2.0" 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth \- Defender\-facing evaluation toolkit: captcha resilience / browser stealth / VPN rotation / adaptive scraping (authorized targets only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defender\-facing evaluation toolkit: captcha resilience / browser stealth / VPN rotation / adaptive scraping (authorized targets only)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format for agent / human consumers. Default `human`; pass `json` for machine\-parseable output.

v1.3 Lane G.4: the global flag remains `\-\-format` (Human|Json) for backward compatibility with v1.2.x. Most subcommands also expose a per\-subcommand `\-\-output\-format` flag with the same value enum, which shadows the global within the subtree. Two subcommands extend the enum locally — `doctor \-\-output\-format {json|text}` and `config \-\-output\-format {text|json|yaml}` — because those surfaces pre\-date the unified flag. The full matrix and JSON schemas live under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/`.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose logging (`\-v`, `\-vv`, `\-vvv`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rev\-stealth\-captcha(1)
CAPTCHA bypass operations (reCAPTCHA v2 / v3 / hCaptcha / Turnstile)
.TP
rev\-stealth\-browser(1)
Stealth browser operations (launch a profile, run a stealth\-test sweep)
.TP
rev\-stealth\-vpn(1)
VPN IP rotation operations (Surfshark / Gluetun lazy\-rotate\-on\-fail)
.TP
rev\-stealth\-doctor(1)
Pre\-flight leak\-prevention checks (kill\-switch / DNS / IPv6 / WebRTC). Exits with code 7 when any check fails (fail\-closed)
.TP
rev\-stealth\-spider(1)
AUP\-gated browse + optional CF eval + optional adaptive relocate
.TP
rev\-stealth\-relocate(1)
Locate a previously fingerprinted element in a saved HTML or fresh URL
.TP
rev\-stealth\-cf\-evaluate(1)
Defender\-testbed evaluation of Cloudflare Turnstile resilience
.TP
rev\-stealth\-auth(1)
Authenticated session capture / lifecycle (Phase 9d). Subcommands: login / list / show / delete / status / refresh
.TP
rev\-stealth\-measure(1)
v1.1.0 (P15): local fingerprint diagnostics for monitoring. External SaaS calls are opt\-in via `\-\-enable\-external`
.TP
rev\-stealth\-config(1)
v1.2.0 (P6.1): inspect the layered config (`show` / `paths` / `validate` / `diff` / `get`)
.TP
rev\-stealth\-hermes(1)
v1.2.0 (P7.3): manage the Hermes plugin scaffold (`install` / `uninstall` / `verify`)
.SH VERSION
v1.2.0
